hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2843","\nNarrated to us Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi, narrated to us Yahya meaning Ibn Sa'id. And narrated to us 'Ali ibn Khashram, informed us 'Isa meaning Ibn Yunus, all from Ibn Jurayj, who said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me, he said: Abu Ma'bad informed me, on the authority of Ibn 'Abbas, on the authority of al-Fadl (RA), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said on the evening of 'Arafah and the morning of Muzdalifah when the people set out:\n\n\Upon you is tranquility (al-sakinah).\"" And he restrained his camel."""""
